From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:42:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-sync): retire audited fenced phantom event uploads
 [daveey]

Why: live_claim restoration intentionally tombstones a phantom lifecycle event, but generic rejection resolution vetoes that tombstone forever. Add a narrow primary-only retirement proof using fresh never-existed Board evidence, a matching rejection audit and compare-and-delete local revalidation. Leave audit, tombstone and worker lease untouched; never replay historical intent.

Proof: normal-sync regression failed before the fix and passes after it; negative predicate and provenance-race controls; each permissive atom removal is killed. Live read-only replay at authenticated empty head 3579946 selects only the incident event. Recovery remains gated on review, CI and normal deployment.
